  fhir:text [
     fhir:status [ fhir:v "generated" ] ;
     fhir:div [ fhir:v "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem medicinal-product-type</b></p><a name=\"medicinal-product-type\"> </a><a name=\"hcmedicinal-product-type\"> </a><div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #d9e0e7; padding: 6px; margin: 4px; border: 1px solid #8da1b4; border-radius: 5px; line-height: 60%\"><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px\">Last updated: 2021-01-05T10:01:24.148+11:00</p></div><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://hl7.org/fhir/medicinal-product-type</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">MedicinalProduct<a name=\"medicinal-product-type-MedicinalProduct\"> </a></td><td>Medicinal Product</td><td>Any substance or combination of substances that may be administered to human beings (or animals) for treating or preventing disease, or with the intent to make a medical diagnosis or to restore, correct or modify physiological functions. Its regulatory status is authorized/marketed for commercial use.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">InvestigationalProduct<a name=\"medicinal-product-type-InvestigationalProduct\"> </a></td><td>Investigational Medicinal Product</td><td>A medicinal product which is being tested or used as a reference, including as a placebo, in a clinical trial. Its regulatory status is under evaluation in a clinical trial; might or might not have marketing authorization.</td></tr></table></div>"^^rdf:XMLLiteral ]
